// ============================================================================
// DVSM META-KERNEL :: CORE EXECUTION CLARIFICATION (REFERENCE EDIT)
// ============================================================================
//
// DESCRIPTION (REFINED):
// A deterministic fixed-point ECS simulation and networking kernel designed to
// produce reproducible, bit-consistent state transitions across all executions.
//
// CORE DESIGN OBJECTIVE:
// Guarantee that identical inputs + identical initial state always produce
// identical outputs and state evolution across all machines, architectures,
// and runtime environments.
//
// This is achieved through:
// - strict Q32.32 fixed-point arithmetic (no floating-point variance)
// - ordered command buffering (no nondeterministic scheduling)
// - deterministic ECS iteration rules (stable indexing / no undefined order)
// - cryptographic state identity function (S_ECHO)
//
// ============================================================================
// CORE EXECUTION MODEL (FORMALIZED)
// ============================================================================
//
// STATE TRANSITION:
//
//     STATE(t+1) = Ξ(INPUT(t), STATE(t))
//
// WHERE:
//
// Ξ = deterministic execution kernel
// INPUT = ordered command stream (L3 enforced ordering)
// STATE = fully serializable ECS state
//
// ============================================================================
// STATE IDENTITY / VALIDITY LAYER
// ============================================================================
//
// Deterministic correctness is verified via:
//
//     HASH(t) = S_ECHO(STATE(t))
//
// EQUALITY RULE:
//
//     STATE_A ≡ STATE_B  ⇔  S_ECHO(STATE_A) == S_ECHO(STATE_B)
//
// PURPOSE:
// Converts runtime correctness from probabilistic simulation agreement
// into cryptographic identity equivalence.
//
// ============================================================================
// PRACTICAL INTERPRETATION
// ============================================================================
//
// - Same input stream → same simulation everywhere
// - No reliance on timing, thread scheduling, or hardware behavior
// - Divergence is always detectable via hash mismatch
// - Recovery is performed via deterministic replay, not heuristics
===============================================================================

PRIMARY SYSTEM PROPERTIES:

1. DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION
- Strict Q32.32 fixed-point arithmetic
- No floating-point dependency
- No nondeterministic iteration or timing reliance

2. LOCKSTEP INPUT PROCESSING
- All commands are buffered and executed in total order
- Ordering governed by deterministic sequencing rules (L3 model)

3. STATE FINALITY VIA S_ECHO
- Each simulation state is reduced to a canonical hash
- S_ECHO(state) defines identity equivalence across nodes
- Hash equality implies state equivalence

4. DISTRIBUTED CONSISTENCY MODEL
- Nodes operate independently but converge on identical state outputs
- Consensus is derived from hash agreement, not probabilistic voting

5. ROLLBACK-FREE RECONSTRUCTION MODEL
- State recovery is performed via deterministic replay
- No snapshot divergence or nondeterministic correction paths

