// I. CORE AXIOM (REFINED ENGINEERING INTERPRETATION)
// ============================================================================
//
// The DVSM system is grounded in a single invariance principle governing
// all execution layers of the runtime model.
//
// FORMAL AXIOM:
//
//     Φ(L1) = Φ(L3) = Φ(L4) = Φ(L5) = ... = Φ(L∞)
//
// WHERE:
//
// Φ  = deterministic state embedding function
//      (maps raw ECS + execution state into canonical identity space)
//
// Lx = execution layers of the system (runtime, consensus, verification,
//      structural validation, and historical continuity layers)
//
// EQUALITY SEMANTICS:
// - equality is strict identity equivalence
// - not probabilistic similarity
// - not numerical approximation
// - not statistical convergence
//
// ============================================================================
// ENGINEERING INTERPRETATION
// ============================================================================
//
// This axiom defines a multi-layer consistency constraint:
//
// All validated system layers must produce the same canonical identity
// representation of state when evaluated through Φ.
//
// In practical terms:
//
// - execution correctness is not defined per-layer
// - correctness is defined by global convergence of identity outputs
//
// ============================================================================
// STATE VALIDITY CONDITION (IMPLEMENTABLE FORM)
// ============================================================================
//
// A system state is considered valid iff:
//
//     1. It is produced by deterministic execution (Ξ)
//     2. It passes cryptographic identity validation (S_ECHO)
//     3. All active system layers produce matching Φ projections
//
// ============================================================================
// SIMPLIFIED MEANING (FOR IMPLEMENTERS)
// ============================================================================
//
// A state is valid when:
//
// - it was computed deterministically
// - it hashes consistently
// - every verification layer agrees on the same result
//
// ============================================================================
// END CORE AXIOM
