// ============================================================================
// ENGINEERING SUMMARY
// ============================================================================
//
// The layer stack defines a deterministic verification hierarchy:
//
// - L1–L3: execution correctness (how state is produced)
// - L4–L5: validation and consensus (how state is accepted)
// - L6–L9: structural + forensic integrity (how state evolves safely)
// - L∞   : historical immutability (how state is remembered)
